  Mountthe same image as both /dd and /h0 and they all find their files:    OS9DISK=<this disk>  OS9H0=<this disk>  os9exec ...OS-9 filenames are case-insensitive, so /h0/games/hack/playgroundfinds GAMES/HACK/playground.SEVEN PROGRAMS USE SNOBOL4-in-C, Robert Heller's C library thatsimulates SNOBOL4's pattern matcher, with programs translated out ofGimpel's "Algorithms in SNOBOL4".  Each is an ordinary 68k program.The library and its makefile are in SRC/effo_snobol, the package's ownnotes in DOC/snobol.  blackjak, poker, rpoem, rstory, rstory2, stoneand tformat are the seven.larn resolves the same way: it wants /h0/GAMES/larn/PLAYGROUND, andGAMES/LARN/PLAYGROUND is on the disk.  It holds the scoreboard larnwrites there for itself, plus .larn.help, .lfortune and .larnmaze.larn plays: it lays out a level, shows its '?' help, keeps score andtakes commands.Those three data files came from the larn 12.2p4 sources; the binaryreports 12.0.  SOURCES.txt records where they came from.  Its siblingularn is complete and also runs.  gnuchessc and gnuan read their datafrom GNUCHESS4.0/MISC and both start.DOC/DEPENDS lists, per program, every absolute path its binarycarries -- read it before copying single commands elsewhere.See DOC/REBUILT-NOTES.md for four curated binaries that wereoverwritten during installation and what was done about each.------------------------------------------------------/dd/CMDS -- added utilities (343)------------------------------------------------------  X11R6shl       X11R6 shared library loader  about          what this collection knows about a program: what it is,                 what it is for, where it came from, the files it opens                 and whether they are here, and whether its source and                 documentation survived.  One card per program --                 `about hack'.  DOC/CATEGORIES browses; this answers.  ape            writes GIBBERISH in the style of whatever it is given -- a